message: "If you use this repository or the paper, please cite the paper below."
title: "No Final Save: Identity, Consciousness, and the Machine That Never Shuts Down"
abstract: >-
  A conceptual framework for persistent artificial entities. Argues that the shift from
  session-bounded models to persistent systems with no clean shutdown forces the questions
  of identity and consciousness into sharper form and raises the stakes on control; defends
  a minimal causal-continuity criterion for identity, proves that terminal versus instrumental
  self-preservation is behaviorally underdetermined, and proposes a developmental rather than
  custodial safety model.
